          up: {"title":"How many readings? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"In Paper 1, Items 1 to 7, the listening extract is read twice and you may take notes. Which plan makes the BEST use of the two readings?","options":[{"t":"Write down every word during the first reading so that you can ignore the second reading.","fb":"Trying to write every word is itself a barrier: while you copy one sentence, you miss the next."},{"t":"Answer the questions during the first reading, then use the second reading to check your answers.","fb":"Answering during the first reading means you stop listening, and the ending often changes the meaning or reveals the purpose."},{"t":"During the first reading, note the main idea, structure and tone; between readings, find the gaps; during the second, listen for devices and details, then answer.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Each reading has a job, and you answer only when you have heard the whole extract twice."},{"t":"Just listen during the first reading without writing anything, and take all your notes during the second.","fb":"Listening closely is good, but you are allowed to take notes during both readings. Waiting wastes the chance to note structure and tone first."}]}
